@1 = ~Please, leave us alone.~
@2 = ~Can't you see me and my mistress have a private conversation? Leave us!~
@3 = ~Watch yourselves. This district is strictly outlawed, and if something happens to you, no witnesses shall come to aid your claims.~
@4 = ~What do you mean by outlawed? Why?~
@5 = ~We will be careful.~
@6 = ~River District isn't called the Second Slums without reason. Crime and deviancy are everyday occurrences here, and you shall find no help should you need it. The law avoids this district. I'm the exception, owing to a shortage of warehouse security. The last worker was found drowned, his skull bashed in. They pay me good money to stand guard until a proper replacement is hired.~
@7 = ~Oh, lady of grace. I have yet to meet a princess such as you. Would you grant a handsome man like me the honour of escorting you to a tavern, so that we can...~
@8 = ~An elf of such clean complexion and fine figure is a rare sight in Athkatla... what am I saying? In all of Toril!~
@9 = ~Oh, lady of night, lady of dread, mistress of darkness. Your beauty is matched only by your wit, which I believe I shall experience first-hand.~
@10 = ~A pink-haired beauty such as yourself is truly a rare sight indeed. The way you carry yourself, those eyes in which one could get lost...~
@11 = ~If you find me some young elven blood, make sure to introduce us. I am a man of... exotic tastes.~
@12 = ~I will pretend I didn't hear that. Don't push your luck. Classy women are not that easy.~
@13 = ~(She blushes.) It... it's really sweet of you. I wish we could talk more, but... I think I should go.~
@14 = ~You shall experience more than just my wit, iblith. Mind your tongue if you wish to keep it. Pathetic peasant.~
@15 = ~Ehm, as charming as it is to hear, you might as well stop right there. There is no future in which you and I end up together. No hard feelings.~
@16 = ~What bloody times we live in. I have to clean my own house! I am a man, and this is woman's work! I advise you, think twice before getting married.~
@17 = ~Heeyah... hic. You wan' some beer?! Hic! I'll... grambhr... some brghbmbrr... hic!~
@18 = ~My wife told me there's a brewer somewhere outside Athkatla who sells very cheap alcohol. Since local brews taste like piss, I might pay him a visit. If only the roads weren't so plagued with bandits and other perils.~
@19 = ~What have I done to deserve Umberlee's wrath? My boat sank, then my cousin was eaten by sharks while fishing out at sea. Now, whenever I try to sail, it starts raining all of a sudden. I must have angered her somehow. Mayhap I wasn't the priest she deserved.~
@20 = ~What have I done to deserve Umberlee's wrath? My boat sank, then my cousin was eaten by sharks while fishing out at sea. Now, whenever I try to sail, it starts raining all of a sudden. I must have angered her somehow. Mayhap I wasn't the priest she deserved.~
@21 = ~We each follow our own path, brother.~
@22 = ~Which is precisely why collusion with the Bitch Queen is beyond my understanding.~
@23 = ~I'm worried about my brother. He lives with his family in Imnesvale. Recently, he stopped sending me letters, and I've heard some spooky stories about strange happenings there.~
@24 = ~Ergh! What are you doing here, Leliana? I told you to go and help Father with lunch.~
@25 = ~Erm... what?~
@26 = ~You have mistaken me for someone else.~
@27 = ~Oh, it's you, Ashton! Forgive me... I can't see very well. Old age, you know.~
@28 = ~Never underestimate the bite of a perch. I lost me finger last time I touched the wretched thing.~
@29 = ~Me working day and night, but me not like strangers. Go away.~
@30 = ~If you have permission to use a warehouse, do so quickly.~
@31 = ~Hah, you? I'm in the mood to slit another throat, so if that's what you came for, no need to beg.~
@32 = ~I changed my mind and want to pay. 5050, was it?~
@33 = ~I changed my mind and want to pay. 5050, was it?~
@34 = ~Never mind. I'll leave you in peace.~
@35 = ~I'm tired of this charade. I'll just execute you.~
@36 = ~What is it you want, stranger?~
@37 = ~Nice flute you've got there. Any chance this isn't yours?~
@38 = ~Nothing.~
@39 = ~It isn't yours either. What business is it of yours? Or do you wish to trade? I'm open to negotiations. My last client for the flute had a little... accident. He has a bloody smile carved on his face for all eternity, if you catch my drift.~
@40 = ~Well? Are you buying, or are you looking for trouble?~
@41 = ~I'm willing to pay.~
@42 = ~I think I know what you mean. You'll have a similar smile once I'm done with you. Care to see?~
@43 = ~Splendid. Ten thousand gold coins.~
@44 = ~What?!~
@45 = ~(Sighs.) All right. Nine thousand.~
@46 = ~Four thousand.~
@47 = ~Seven thousand.~
@48 = ~Five thousand.~
@49 = ~Five thousand and fifty. Not a coin less.~
@50 = ~Done.~
@51 = ~No deal.~
@52 = ~I'm tired of this charade. I'll just execute you.~
@53 = ~Pleasure doing business with you. Now, off with you!~
@54 = ~You haven't the coin. Come back when you can afford my price.~
@55 = ~Then the flute stays with me. If you ain't paying, someone else eventually will.~
@56 = ~Stupid, stupid! Your head will roll for this!~
@57 = ~Are we seriously considering doing business with scum like this?~
@58 = ~Turn around and walk away. Stick your nosy nostrils out of our business, peasant.~
@59 = ~I don't like the look of you. Begone!~
@60 = ~I have lost my lucky ring somewhere in this area. If you'd be so kind as to help me find it, I'd be truly grateful.~
@61 = ~Lucky Ring: A young woman named Felicity lost her lucky ring somewhere within the River District. I should hand it over if I find it.~
@62 = ~If you find my lucky ring, please bring it back to me. I would be very grateful.~
@63 = ~Me guard the warehouse! Please, don't be trouble.~
